# SSO Convex environment variables

Set via Convex dashboard or CLI from `src/convex/sso`:

```bash
npx convex env set CLERK_SECRET_KEY sk_test_...
```

# Frontend (repo root `.env.local`)

Run from project root after `clerk auth login` and `clerk link --app app_3Fojpg8n34wLhLwKalH8nPAjhLy`:

```bash
clerk env pull
```

Or set manually:

```bash
VITE_CLERK_PUBLISHABLE_KEY=pk_test_...
```

Clerk player login requires the partner row's **`playerAuth.mode`** to be `clerk` or `embed_then_clerk`, e.g. `{ mode: "clerk" }`.

Platform / Partner admin Web password always uses **`staffAuth.mode = "web"`** (cid=0 identity routing).

Default partner (pid=0) bootstrap:

```bash
node scripts/platform/bootstrap-default-partner-channels.mjs --apply --player-mode clerk
```

In Clerk Dashboard → Paths, allow redirect URLs for your app origin, e.g.:

- `http://localhost:3000/campaign/*` (dev)
- production campaign URLs

OAuth returns to `#/sso-callback` on the current pathname; the app mounts a global callback handler on campaign pages (`auth:0`).

Verify integration:

```bash
clerk doctor
```
